module gunbc.rung_drop.determinism_transitive_reachability

import std.types { NonEmptyStr, List }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { GuaranteeRung, MechanicallyPreventable, Mitigatable }
import gunbc.rung_drop { RungDrop, Standing, TypedDeclaration, DeletedWithoutReplacement }

// RUNG DROP — DETERMINISM TRANSITIVE REACHABILITY (2026-09-05).
//
// The fn-arrow corpus_dependency_view composition (mechanism #2 of the §3 consolidation)
// carried fn-arrow declarations across ~25 lens modules whose call graph the
// determinism_transitive_holds witness walked. Deleting corpus_dependency_view removed
// those declarations' subject modules from the fn_arrow_decl_facts_live acquisition
// (they were under src/v2/lens/affected_set, which also contained the deleted modules).
// As a result, determinism_transitive_live_closure_holds can no longer follow callee
// edges into other modules within budget.
//
// The witness has been renamed to determinism_live_intra_holds to reflect that only
// intra-declaration determinism is checked. No cross-module callee traversal occurs.
// This is a real check of each declaration's own structure but does NOT establish
// that the call graph is determinism-safe.
//
// CAUSE CORRECTED BY MEASUREMENT, 2026-09-07. This row previously attributed the budget
// pressure to the NUMBER OF REACHABLE DECLARATIONS, and that attribution is refuted rather
// than refined: the directory-grain walk this drop is gated on reaches FEWER THAN A HUNDRED
// declarations -- barely more than the 78 it seeds from -- and still costs twenty times the
// per-claim line. The cost is not in the reached set; it is in the CANDIDATE POOL that
// decls_matching_callee rescans for every callee of every reached declaration. The wrong
// sentence has been replaced rather than annotated, because a restoration trigger is the
// whole check: a trigger naming a term that is not the cost is satisfied by nothing, and it
// would stand forever with an honest-looking receipt attached while anyone chasing it
// optimised a quantity that does not move the number.
data determinism_transitive_reachability: RungDrop = RungDrop {
  identity: "determinism_transitive_reachability" as NonEmptyStr,

  subject: "Transitive determinism reachability over the fn-arrow call graph",

  declared: "2026-09-05",

  standing: Standing,

  declaration: TypedDeclaration {
    previous: MechanicallyPreventable,
    temporary: Mitigatable,
    reason: DeletedWithoutReplacement,
    population: [
      "v2.lens.affected_set.corpus_dependency_view (fn-arrow composition, deleted)",
      "v2.lens.affected_set.entry_selection (fn-arrow declarations, deleted)",
    ],
    restoration_trigger: "CAPABILITY: THE CALLEE LOOKUP ANSWERS BY INDEX RATHER THAN BY SCANNING THE CANDIDATE POOL — v2.std.fn_index.decls_matching_callee resolves (module set, callee name) to its matching declarations through an index built once per acquisition, so the walk's cost is a function of the declarations it REACHES and not of the pool it was handed. SUFFICIENT FOR: determinism_transitive_holds with pool_roots=['src/v2/lens'] and pool_files=[] reaching a verdict (Holds or Findings) within the 500ms required_floor_claim_cpu_safety_limit_ms, at directory grain, without narrowing the subject. MEASURED CAUSE, replacing this row's previous attribution to the number of reachable declarations, which is refuted: at directory grain the walk reaches FEWER THAN 100 declarations against a candidate pool of 1500-2000 and costs 10137ms — about 90ms per reached declaration, against 2.9ms per reached declaration at file grain where the pool equals the reached set. The two cost models separate cleanly across the two grains: O(reached x pool) agrees within 1.9x, O(reached squared) disagrees by 44x. The mechanism is that decls_matching_callee runs filter(decls_in_modules(decls, modules), name == callee) — a full scan of the candidate pool plus a module-membership scan — once per callee per reached declaration. At file grain pool equals n, so the shape LOOKS quadratic in the reached set; at directory grain the two decouple and the pool dominates. Re-derive the instrument rather than trusting these figures: claim_batch over a probe calling call_reachable_decls at both grains, bracketing the reached count and the pool size by threshold ladder. BOTH REPAIRS THIS ROW PREVIOUSLY PRESCRIBED ARE REFUTED BY THAT MEASUREMENT AND ARE NAMED HERE SO THEY ARE NOT RE-ATTEMPTED. (i) Reducing PER-DECLARATION cost in determinism_findings or callees_from_node cannot reach the line: the reached population is under 100 and the walk is 10137ms, so even halving per-declaration work leaves seconds. (ii) Scoping pool_roots to exactly the modules reachable from affected_set.dag WOULD lower the number, and that is the trap rather than the repair — it lowers it by SHRINKING THE POOL, leaving the shape intact, and it is the same narrow-the-subject move that created this drop in the first place. A drop retired that way re-breaks the moment the subject widens, and the widening is the thing the drop exists to restore. COST SHAPES IN THIS WALK ARE REAL AND ARE EXPLICITLY NOT THE COST, recorded so a later reader does not fix them and believe the defect is gone. THREE OF THEM ARE NOW REPAIRED and are named in the past tense because their symbols no longer resolve: call_reachable_decls_go scanned `reached` linearly per seed through a decl_in_list helper that is deleted, and now answers membership by keyed lookup over a seen map; it appended to `reached` with a copied accumulator and now conses and reverses once at the end; and list_append(rest, callee_decls) copied the worklist every step and is now guarded so an empty callee list does not copy it. REPAIRING THEM DID NOT RETIRE THIS DROP AND WAS NEVER EXPECTED TO: the pool scan in decls_matching_callee named by this trigger's CAPABILITY clause is untouched, and this row is retired by that capability and by nothing else. ONE SHAPE IN callees_from_node IS AN ADMITTED, UNRESOLVED OBLIGATION rather than a repair: its duplicate suppression is a linear scan of the accumulated list per callee, which is quadratic in the callees of one declaration and is subject to the same bare-minimum-cost rule. A map-keyed arm was written and measured SLOWER than the list scan at the realized callee counts and was reverted on that measurement; big-O did not grant permission to ship the slower realization, and equally the slower first attempt did not retire the defect it was aimed at. The obligation dissolves when the walk is asked at a grain whose per-declaration callee counts are large enough for the keyed arm to win, and it is recorded here rather than in the source so that it is folded with the rest of this row. THE REMAINING UNREPAIRED SHAPES: determinism_transitive_findings folds with concat(acc, determinism_findings(...)), a copied accumulator that is FREE while the corpus is clean and degrades quadratically exactly when findings appear, so it is invisible in every green run and expensive only when something is already wrong. determinism_live_closure_modules folds list_snoc_item over module_declaration_facts_live(pool_roots: []), a copied accumulator over a list that is empty today. Until this trigger fires, determinism over the fn-arrow call graph is unverified.",
  }
}
